    "result_text": "All 3 acceptance tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization in the owner-creation flow, following the existing controller idioms (mirroring how `normalizeTelephone` is applied).\n\n**Changes to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. **New `normalizeAddress` helper** \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). `null` returns `\"\"` (never `null`). Matching whole tokens avoids corrupting words like `STREET` that contain `ST`.\n\n2. **`addOwner`** now normalizes the address up front and:\n   - **Required-field check** uses the normalized value, so an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400 via `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n   - **Household duplicate detection** (`isHouseholdInUse`) receives the normalized address.\n   - The owner is stored with `owner.setAddress(normalizedAddress)`, so the persisted and returned `address` is canonical, and the **shared household id** (`joinHousehold` \u2192 `householdIdFor`, driven by `owner.getAddress()`) is derived from the normalized form.\n\nBecause every created owner now stores the normalized address and every comparison path receives the normalized address, household detection and the shared household identifier are all computed over the normalized form, consistent with the spec.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase` (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`), `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations` (`\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`), and `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize` (`\"   \"` \u2192 400) all green.",
